.TH "AUTOSNAP" "1" "Jun 2026" "autosnap" "autosnap manual"

.SH NAME
autosnap-mark - Mark checkpoints unmarked, good, or bad


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBautosnap mark (--bad|--good|--unmark)  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark one checkpoint or an inclusive checkpoint range unmarked, good, or bad.

.PP
A range A..B marks checkpoints from A through B, inclusive. Ranges are
inclusive autosnap checkpoint intervals, not general Git revision ranges.

.PP
The checkpoint argument can be an explicit autosnap ref, a checkpoint commit hash,
or one of these current-branch history selectors:

.PP
first
  first+N
  last
  last-N


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--bad\fP[=false]
	Mark selected checkpoints bad

.PP
\fB--good\fP[=false]
	Mark selected checkpoints good

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mark

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Human-readable reason for a bad mark

.PP
\fB--unmark\fP[=false]
	Remove explicit good or bad marks from selected checkpoints


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBautosnap(1)\fP
